---
import LegalPage from '~/components/layout/LegalPage.astro';
import { defaultLocale } from '~/i18n/routing';
import { site } from '~/config/site';
import { contactEmail } from '~/lib/contact-email';

const email = contactEmail();
---

<LegalPage
  locale={defaultLocale}
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms for Rarest Answer, a free browser trivia game. No account, and no affiliation with Krillion or other games named here."
  lastUpdated="2026-11-14"
>
  <p>
    By using {site.game.name}, you agree to these terms. The game is free to play in the browser.
    There is no account.
  </p>
  <h2>The game</h2>
  <p>
    A prompt asks you to name something that fits. An accepted answer is correct. A rarer correct
    answer scores more. A daily round is seven shared prompts and resets at local midnight.
    Unlimited play and single-category play use the same tiers. The points table, Spotlight (one
    double per round), and the timer switch are described on
    <a href="/guides/how-to-play-rarest-answer/">how to play</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Streak and round stats stay in localStorage on this device. You can clear them in the browser.
    We do not restore a streak from another device, because there is no account to restore it from.
  </p>
  <h2>Use of the site</h2>
  <p>
    Guides, prompt pages, and the game are for personal use. You may quote a page if you credit it
    and link to the original URL. Do not copy the site and present it as your own game.
  </p>
  <h2>Scores and accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    A tier is a rank inside that prompt's answer list. It is computed from the popularity number
    stored with the answer. On the published prompts, that number is a Wikipedia pageview count, or
    a Wiktionary pageview count for the English interjection list. A prompt whose
    <code>source</code> is <code>fixture</code> would still have placeholder numbers. None of the
    published prompts use that label. Rankings change when the dataset is rebuilt. A score is not a
    scientific ranking, a box-office ranking, or a claim that one real-world thing is "better" than
    another.
  </p>
  <p>
    We try to keep guides accurate. A rule that a public page does not state is left out rather
    than filled in. Game updates and dataset rebuilds can make a page stale. Check the date on the
    page, and check the prompt's <code>source</code> field before you treat a rarity order as a
    measured pageview rank.
  </p>
  <h2>Other games</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalNotice} {site.game.name} is not affiliated with Krillion or with any other game
    named on this site, and it is not endorsed by the people who make those games. Names are used
    so you can tell the products apart.
  </p>
  <h2>Third-party services and links</h2>
  <p>
    Pages may link to other sites. We do not control those sites. Advertising, analytics, and
    comments load only when the matching environment variables are set. What they receive is
    described in the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>. When comments are enabled,
    GitHub's terms apply to the GitHub account you use to post.
  </p>
  <h2>Trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    Krillion and the other game names, logos, and characters mentioned on this site belong to
    their owners. {site.game.name} claims no ownership of those marks. The tier names Common,
    Familiar, Uncommon, Rare, Epic, and Legendary, and the boost name Spotlight, are labels this
    game uses for its own scoring. They are not the tier names of another product.
  </p>
  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided as-is. Use it at your own risk. We are not liable for damages arising
    from your use of the site or from relying on a score, a guide, or a rarity order.
  </p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may revise these terms by posting the new text on this page. The date under the title is
    the revision date.
  </p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
